Adds JitRiscV64NoMemoryBarriers (default 1): the riscv64 JIT emits no `fence`. A single-hart zkVM guest
(ZisK, SP1, OpenVM) has no other hart, device or asynchronous observer of memory, so a barrier orders
nothing - but each is one executed step, and the JIT emits one before every volatile load/store (which
includes the static-base initialization check on every access to a static of a type with a cctor: ~2500
`fence rw,rw` in ~1300 functions of the Nethermind guest) and for every Interlocked.MemoryBarrier /
Volatile.* call. Every barrier the JIT emits goes through CodeGen::instGen_MemoryBarrier, which now returns
early when the knob is set. Set JitRiscV64NoMemoryBarriers=0 on any target where another agent can observe
memory.

RISC-V64: JitRiscV64NoMemoryBarriers (default 1) - emit no fence; zkVM guests are single-hart.

diff --git a/src/coreclr/jit/codegenriscv64.cpp b/src/coreclr/jit/codegenriscv64.cpp
index 0d4f8702b..8d5bae87d 100644
--- a/src/coreclr/jit/codegenriscv64.cpp
+++ b/src/coreclr/jit/codegenriscv64.cpp
@@ -6881,6 +6881,14 @@ void CodeGen::instGen_MemoryBarrier(BarrierKind barrierKind)
     }
 #endif // DEBUG
 
+    // zkVM: a single-hart guest with no asynchronous observer of memory; a fence
+    // orders nothing and costs a step. Every barrier the JIT emits goes through
+    // here (volatile indirs, GT_MEMORYBARRIER, volatile block ops).
+    if (JitConfig.JitRiscV64NoMemoryBarriers() != 0)
+    {
+        return;
+    }
+
     insBarrier barrier;
     switch (barrierKind)
     {
diff --git a/src/coreclr/jit/jitconfigvalues.h b/src/coreclr/jit/jitconfigvalues.h
index 63ccaf18a..fd3f839c3 100644
--- a/src/coreclr/jit/jitconfigvalues.h
+++ b/src/coreclr/jit/jitconfigvalues.h
@@ -511,6 +511,14 @@ RELEASE_CONFIG_INTEGER(JitNoUnalignedAccess,        "JitNoUnalignedAccess",
 // locals and statics are provably aligned and stay single instructions. For zkVMs
 // that reject any misaligned access (SP1, OpenVM). Off by default.
 RELEASE_CONFIG_INTEGER(JitRiscV64StrictAlign,       "JitRiscV64StrictAlign",     0)
+// Single-hart zkVM guests (ZisK, SP1, OpenVM): there is no other hart, no device
+// and no asynchronous observer of memory, so a memory barrier orders nothing -
+// but every `fence` is still one executed step, and the JIT emits one before every
+// volatile load/store (which includes the static-base initialization check on
+// each access to a static of a type with a cctor) and for every
+// Interlocked.MemoryBarrier / Volatile.* call. When 1, the riscv64 JIT emits no
+// `fence` at all. Set 0 on any target where another agent can observe memory.
+RELEASE_CONFIG_INTEGER(JitRiscV64NoMemoryBarriers,  "JitRiscV64NoMemoryBarriers", 1)
 #endif
 
 RELEASE_CONFIG_INTEGER(EnableEmbeddedBroadcast,     "EnableEmbeddedBroadcast",   1) // Allows embedded broadcasts to be disabled
